# Demo Visual Validation Rules

## TL;DR — The one command you need

```bash
npx playwright test e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts --reporter=html
```

The HTML report opens automatically. Every assertion and screenshot is inline.
Run it, fix failures, run it again. **Never trial-and-error through Playwright MCP.**

---

## The Problem This Rule Solves

Agents repeatedly "visually validate" demos by:
1. Using `browser_evaluate` / `browser_click` Playwright MCP calls in a loop
2. Hardcoding `await sleep(1200)` instead of proper waits
3. Rediscovering the same DOM selectors from scratch every session
4. Taking ad-hoc screenshots with no consistent naming or location

This is slow, fragile, and produces zero reusable artifacts.

---

## The Right Way: Playwright E2E Specs

### Existing infrastructure

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `e2e/demo-player-helpers.ts` | All reusable helpers (launch, advance, assert, screenshot) |
| `e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts` | Step-through spec for WS Workflow Builder |
| `e2e/demo-hub-validate.spec.ts` | All 34 lessons: launch + concept + first-step validation |

### Key helpers (always import from `./demo-player-helpers`)

```typescript
// Full navigation: Demo Hub → category → lesson → Start
await launchLesson(page, 'WebSocket', 'Workflow Builder');

// Advance N complete steps (runs each action, waits for reading phase)
await advanceSteps(page, 3);

// Run one step action and wait for completion — THE canonical step advance
await runNextStep(page);

// THE canonical synchronisation gate — use instead of any sleep()
await waitForReadingPhase(page);

// Assert a ReactFlow node is NOT selected (no blue ring)
await assertNodeNotSelected(page, '.react-flow__node-wsConnect');

// Assert config modal is open / closed
await assertConfigModalOpen(page);
await assertConfigModalClosed(page);

// Take a screenshot with a meaningful name (saved to e2e/screenshots/)
await takeNamedScreenshot(page, 'step-4-config-modal-no-ring');
```

---

## When to Create / Update a Spec

### Always create/update a spec when you:
- Fix a visual bug in a demo lesson (step order, highlight, modal state)
- Add or restructure steps in any lesson file
- Change `preAction` / `action` logic that affects visible behaviour

### The spec must verify the specific fix:

```typescript
// Example: the "node highlighted inside config modal" fix
test('config modal opens without node selection ring', async ({ page }) => {
  await launchLesson(page, 'WebSocket', 'Workflow Builder');
  await advanceSteps(page, 3);  // reach step 4 reading phase
  await page.locator('[aria-label="Next step"]').click();
  await page.waitForSelector('.wf-config-modal');  // intercept mid-action
  await assertNodeNotSelected(page, '.react-flow__node-wsConnect');
});
```

---

## When to Add a New Spec File

Each lesson that has had substantive fixes should get its own spec:

```
e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts    ← exists
e2e/demo-kafka-consume.spec.ts          ← create when fixing Consume Studio
e2e/demo-kafka-headers.spec.ts          ← create when fixing Headers & Filters
e2e/demo-sse-advanced.spec.ts           ← create when fixing SSE Advanced
```

Name pattern: `e2e/demo-{protocol}-{lesson-slug}.spec.ts`

## These specs are EXCLUDED from the normal E2E suite

Step-through specs (`demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts` and all future
`demo-{protocol}-*.spec.ts` files) are listed in `DEMO_STEPTHROUGH_SPECS`
inside `playwright.config.ts`. They are excluded from the default `chromium`
project because they run for 40–60s per test and are only relevant when
fixing demo lessons.

- `npx playwright test` — does NOT run these
- `npx playwright test e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts --reporter=html` — runs them explicitly

When you add a new step-through spec, add it to `DEMO_STEPTHROUGH_SPECS`
in `playwright.config.ts` so it stays excluded from the normal suite.

---

## Run Commands

```bash
# Single lesson
npx playwright test e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts --reporter=html

# All demo specs
npx playwright test e2e/demo-*.spec.ts --reporter=html

# Full hub validation (all 34 lessons, concept + first-step only)
npx playwright test e2e/demo-hub-validate.spec.ts --reporter=html

# With increased timeout for slow steps
npx playwright test e2e/demo-ws-workflow-builder.spec.ts --reporter=html --timeout=60000
```

The `--reporter=html` flag is **mandatory** per the E2E testing rules. It produces
a browsable report at `playwright-report/index.html`.

